@page "/docs/components/collapsible"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Collapsible
<PageTitle>Collapsible - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Collapsible</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="collapsible" />
        </div>
        <p>A section that shows and hides its content with a height animation, leaving the look of the trigger entirely to you. The trigger sets <code>aria-expanded</code>, so your own icons can react to it with plain CSS. Set <code>KeepRendered</code> on the content when the components inside should keep their state while closed.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(CollapsibleUsageExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, compose a trigger and content. The trigger is usually a `BzButton` passed through `RenderAs`, and the panel animates open and closed." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of a collapsible: a trigger, which can be your own element through `RenderAs`, and a content panel that animates open and closed." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="Anything placed outside `BzCollapsibleContent` stays visible. Only the rows inside open and close with the trigger." Example="typeof(CollapsibleDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom trigger (RenderAs)" Description="Use `RenderAs` to make the trigger an element of your own, here an anchor, and apply the attributes it provides to that element." Example="typeof(CollapsibleRenderAsTriggerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Open by default" Description="Set `DefaultOpen` to start expanded." Example="typeof(CollapsibleDefaultOpenExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Description="Set `Disabled` to block toggling. The trigger is dimmed to show it." Example="typeof(CollapsibleDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom indicator" Description="Swap icons based on the trigger's `aria-expanded` state, the same way the accordion turns its chevron." Example="typeof(CollapsibleIndicatorExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled" Description="Bind `Open` two-way when other code needs to read or change whether the section is open." Example="typeof(CollapsibleControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Every part accepts `Class`. Here the trigger is a full-width indigo pill and the rows get a tinted border. The trigger is your own button, so you style it directly."
          Example="typeof(CollapsibleCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the trigger, the padding and the rows all move to the opposite side." Example="typeof(CollapsibleRtlExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzCollapsible",
        new CompositionNode("BzCollapsibleTrigger"),
        new CompositionNode("BzCollapsibleContent"));
}
